FINAL INSIGHTS :- 
🔍 Insight 1: Traders perform significantly better during Fear than Greed
Average daily PnL during Fear is substantially higher than during Greed and Neutral periods.
This suggests that volatility during Fear creates more profitable trading opportunities for active traders.

🔍 Insight 2: Trade frequency increases during Fear and Extreme Greed
Traders execute ~4x more trades during Fear compared to Greed days.
Extreme Greed days show very large average trade sizes, indicating aggressive positioning.

🔍 Insight 3: Position sizing decreases as sentiment turns cautious
During Neutral and Greed days, traders reduce average position size.
This indicates risk-off behavior and lower conviction trades during calmer market phases.
